ests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Dina Titus (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Dina Titus, a long-serving Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in a Las Vegas-based district that leans Democratic by about two points. No general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and expert judgment. Ten ratings outlets place the race at Likely D or better, and prediction markets give Titus roughly a 95% chance of winning.\n\nRepublican Carrie Buck has run a serious campaign, raising about $2.6 million and drawing support from national figures including the House speaker, and some observers see Nevada Republicans outperforming a difficult national map. Still, the district's lean, Titus's incumbency, and the weight of expert and market evidence point to a Democratic hold with a double-digit expected margin, though with meaningful uncertainty given the absence of polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9485, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9231, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9459, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9451, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9504, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9463, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9234, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9304, "margin": 10.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9333, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9462, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9264, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9326, "